What I call end-game: From the turn you use the magic portal to enter
Rodney's tower until ascension or death.  The biggest problems cycle
among Rodney, spell casters, summon storms, and then riders and
artifact-wielding player-monsters.

What I call late-game: A boundary somewhere near the Castle and VotD.
I basically figure the late-game is when you're fully kitted to handle
Gehenome and maybe you've built up a stash that will be used on the
way out.  Maybe it starts when you use the Castle wand, maybe when
you decide you don't need the wishes so you do down below the VotD.
During the late-game demons are the major enemy.  Summoning demons
and spellcasting demons put you at risk of dying.

What I call mid-game: Castle/VotD at the bottom, Medusa, Quest,
Ludios and such.  Angels appear and are a major obstacle unless
they are peacefull and you avoid them.

What I call the early-game: Through completion of the mines and
Sokoban.



